A statement written on the same line after a standalone comment moves to
its own line, so code cannot hide behind a comment (fmt.indent_style
issue #101); the statement takes the block indent like any other.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Demo;
:DECLARE nValue;
/* initialize; nValue := 1;
:IF nValue > 0;
/* bump it;nValue += 1;
:ENDIF;
:RETURN nValue;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Demo;
	:DECLARE nValue;
	/* initialize;
	nValue := 1;
	:IF nValue > 0;
		/* bump it;
		nValue += 1;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN nValue;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
3:1-3:15 warning comment_text_after_terminator: Comment terminated early by semicolon. Text after the ';' becomes executable code and may be unintentionally hidden
5:1-5:12 warning comment_text_after_terminator: Comment terminated early by semicolon. Text after the ';' becomes executable code and may be unintentionally hidden
